WEBVTT

00:38:26.506 --> 00:38:30.654
But she also was the most
forgiving human being I've ever met.

00:38:30.678 --> 00:38:32.460
And when I asked her one time,

00:38:32.484 --> 00:38:36.084
"Why are you so forgiving?
You have such a capacity to forgive."

00:38:36.108 --> 00:38:40.273
She said, "I've had to beg forgiveness
from so many people

00:38:40.297 --> 00:38:42.915
for things that I've done,
and they've given it to me,

00:38:42.939 --> 00:38:45.256
that forgiveness and mercy
are what I owe."

00:38:45.280 --> 00:38:47.013
And I was her best friend.

00:38:47.037 --> 00:38:50.046
I mean, we were best friends
for years and years and years,

00:38:50.070 --> 00:38:54.574
but I was always kind of in love with her,
but I just kept the boundary,

00:38:54.598 --> 00:38:58.046
because I was married,
and I didn't want to cross that boundary.

00:38:58.070 --> 00:39:00.210
And then she got sick,
and then it was like,